---
title: "update_randomness_state (Sui Framework: random)"
---
stateDiagram-v2
    direction TB
    [*] --> q_check_sender: assert ctx.sender() == @0x0
    q_check_sender --> q_abort_sender: sender != system
    q_abort_sender --> [*]: abort ENotSystemAddress
    q_check_sender --> q_load_inner: system address
    q_load_inner --> q_check_first: check if first update
    q_check_first --> q_first_update: round==0, epoch==0, bytes empty
    q_first_update --> q_check_first_round: assert new_round == 0
    q_check_first_round --> q_abort_round: new_round != 0
    q_abort_round --> [*]: abort EInvalidRandomnessUpdate
    q_check_first --> q_subsequent: not first update
    q_subsequent --> q_check_valid: epoch > inner.epoch AND new_round == 0 OR new_round == inner.round + 1
    q_check_valid --> q_abort_valid: neither condition met
    q_abort_valid --> [*]: abort EInvalidRandomnessUpdate
    q_check_valid --> q_update: valid update
    q_check_first_round --> q_update: first round valid
    q_update --> q_set_values: inner.epoch = ctx.epoch()
    q_set_values --> q_set_round: inner.randomness_round = new_round
    q_set_round --> q_set_bytes: inner.random_bytes = new_bytes
    q_set_bytes --> [*]: randomness state updated

    note right of q_check_sender
        INV-001: only system address (@0x0) can update randomness
        INV-002: rounds must be monotonically increasing within epoch
        INV-003: new epoch resets round to 0
        INV-004: epoch can skip if no randomness generated in intermediate epochs
    end note
